              "Common errors in technical writing cluster into a short list. Subject-verb agreement slips: 'the data shows' vs 'the data show' (be consistent). Article errors: 'I am engineer' (missing 'an'), 'the India' (extra 'the'), 'a university' vs 'an university' (sound-based). Tense errors: 'the experiment will showed' (mixed), 'last year the team has tested' (present perfect with past time). Preposition errors: 'different than' (from), 'comprise of' (comprise, no 'of'; or 'is composed of'), 'discuss about' (discuss, no 'about'), 'repeat again' (tautology). Word choice: 'affect' vs 'effect', 'principal' vs 'principle', 'loose' vs 'lose', 'stationary' vs 'stationery'. Punctuation: comma splices joining two complete sentences with a comma (use a semicolon or full stop); missing apostrophes in possessives ('the engineer's report' not 'the engineers report').",
